    "abstract": "Purpose \u2013 The study explores rising climate fluctuations in Kazakhstan, focusing on agriculture\u2019s resilience; it highlights consequences for income security, village communities, or future planning. Methodology \u2013 This research uses descriptive methods alongside comparison techniques, relying on existing data. It examines patterns in rising temperatures, shifts in rainfall, more frequent droughts, declining soil quality, or limited water access. These environmental factors are then connected to how well farming performs over time. Originality / value \u2013 The study adds to existing work on climate risks in Central Asia by linking environmental, financial, and sector-level factors into one analysis approach while using varied structural choices per sentence. A rare look at how farming and climate interact in Kazakhstan is provided, showing local adaptation efforts already tested in real conditions instead of relying on generic solutions. Findings \u2013 Results indicate rising heat stress, less rain, frequent droughts, and growing dry areas reduce crop output, animal performance, or soil health, thus harming food access plus income in rural regions. The study highlights key adaptive actions like smart irrigation tools, varied farming setups, or sturdy equipment and methods which may improve resistance while aiding lasting growth.",
    "field": "Climate change and agriculture",
    "problem": "Climate change in Kazakhstan\u2014characterized by rising temperatures, frequent droughts, and water scarcity\u2014is reducing crop yields and livestock productivity, degrading soil and water resources, and threatening the resilience of the agricultural sector, food security, and rural incomes.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a policy roadmap for adapting Kazakhstan's agriculture to climate change by integrating multiple strategies, including smart irrigation, drought-tolerant crop selection, institutional support, and strong farmer participation.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze the impact of climate change on agriculture in Kazakhstan, examining consequences for production and identifying key adaptive actions to improve resilience and ensure sustainable economic development.",
